"""
OpenAI-compatible API slot router. Configure every slot via LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_* env vars.
No IP addresses or ports are hardcoded — all local service addresses come from .env with
localhost defaults. Cloud API endpoints use their public URLs as defaults.

Local slots (LMSTUDIO, WINDOWS_NPU) do NOT require an API key — they are treated as keyless.
For LAN access (e.g. Quest 3 reaching the host PC), set LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_WINDOWS_NPU_BASE_URL
or LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL to the LAN IP in .env.

Env var pattern per slot PREFIX (OPENAI, GEMINI, EXTRA, LMSTUDIO, OLLAMA, OPENROUTER, VENICE, GITHUB, WINDOWS_NPU):
  LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_{PREFIX}_API_KEY   — API key (required for cloud slots, optional for local)
  LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_{PREFIX}_BASE_URL  — Override base URL (falls back to public API default)
  LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_{PREFIX}_MODEL     — Model name (slot-specific defaults apply)
  LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_{PREFIX}_LABEL     — Display label

Additional fallbacks for specific slots:
  OLLAMA:     OLLAMA_API_KEY, LUMAX_CLOUD_BASE_URL, LUMAX_MODEL_CLOUD_ID
  LMSTUDIO:   LMSTUDIO_MAIN_MODEL
  WINDOWS_NPU: (uses windows-npu-phi-silica as default model)

OpenAI pay-as-you-go guard:
  LUMAX_OPENAI_DAILY_MAX_REQUESTS — if > 0, cap successful OpenAI-slot calls per UTC day (state file).
  LUMAX_OPENAI_USAGE_STATE_PATH — optional JSON counter file (default: system temp dir).
  LUMAX_REPERTOIRE_OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS — optional lower max_tokens for OpenAI slot only.
Also set hard limits in the OpenAI / Azure dashboard where available; this is a local safety net.

Cloud completion length:
  LUMAX_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS — default max_tokens for /chat/completions when callers do not pass max_tokens.
  LUMAX_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS_CAP — upper clamp for max_tokens (default 131072 if unset). Set lower (e.g. 8192)
  on small models or tight budgets.
"""
